# X5H (R-Car Gen5) NDA working directories -- NEVER commit anything from these.
# They hold Renesas R-Car xOS SDK material: rcar_gen5_mp_phy.bin, the
# firmware-embedding Image-autosd built from it, board serial-session logs and
# site-specific handoff notes. The hard NDA boundary for this platform is that
# no blob, and no kernel image embedding one, ever reaches this repo, CI, CI
# logs or CI artifacts (see platforms/autosd/x5h/README.md, "The firmware
# split"). Ignoring them makes a reflexive `git add -A` mid board session
# unable to stage an NDA binary, instead of relying on operator discipline.
/x5h-work/
/x5h/
# R-Car xOS Platform SDK v4.35.0 extraction (samples, manuals, prebuilt CR52
# ELFs) unpacked at the repo root on 2026-08-06 so the host PC can browse the
# vendor docs. Same hard NDA boundary and reflexive-`git add -A` guard as
# /x5h/ above: nothing under it may ever be staged.
/rcar-xos/
/CES2026/
/tmux-x5h-*.log
# Unverified-provenance archive picked up mid board session; "safety island"
# is an X5H/R-Car subsystem name so it may hold NDA material -- never opened,
# never staged, ignored on the same reflexive-`git add -A` grounds as above.
/home-test-youtalk-autoware-safety-island.zip

# Superpowers SDD working artifacts: specs, plans, review reports, progress
# ledgers and range diffs. Project convention keeps these OUT of the target
# repo -- they belong under ~/src/claude-superpowers -- so this is the same
# reflexive-`git add -A` guard as the directories above, not an NDA one.
# Nothing under here has ever been tracked.
/.superpowers/
